{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1790523000002-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice8-confirm-r3.gpt-6-sol.findings.md; cat collab/1790530211570-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice8-fixes-r3.glm-flash.report.md'","aggregated_output":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-27 19:09:01 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-28 02:09:01 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\nThe two original P1s are addressed: lowered link waits use the engine’s fixed keys, and the retained FFI request now carries a response route. The supplied focused results are green; I did not rerun suites or edit files.\n\n**P1 — retained-call routing overwrites the receiver’s call pair.** `lower-frame` installs the emitter’s reflected call streams and route cell at the receiver’s fixed keys ([remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:531), [remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:562), [remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:737)). Those are also the keys used by calls the resumed program makes later. The [UCF routing rule](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:614) requires the outstanding call to use the emitter’s pair while future calls use the receiver’s own pair. The new resume test ([remote_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:499)) ends after the migrated call, so it does not exercise that collision.\n\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES\nSign-off: DENIEDThe route-cell routing fix (P1 from gate r3).** The wholesale replacement of the receiver's fixed call-pair keys is gone, and the outstanding call now routes to the emitter's pair entirely through non-fixed state:\n\n- Deleted `call-pair-resources` outright — `lower-frame` (src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:712-716) no longer installs the emitter's reflected call streams at `vm/call-in-stream-key`/`vm/call-out-stream-key`. Those keys remain the receiving composition's own supply (`ffi/call-pair`, ffi.cljc:33-40), so the resumed program's future FFI calls use the receiver's own pair (UCF §\"Outstanding calls route to the emitter's pair; the resumer's pair is its own\", yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:614-624).\n- The lowered `:request-sent` entry's `:stream-id` is the fresh reflection key of the emitter's own call-in (remote.cljc:648) — the retry appends on the emitter's pair without occupying the fixed call-in key (remote.cljc:641-661).\n- The route cell lowers as the fixed `vm/call-out-cursor-key` entry — the one key the restored response wait reads (`semantic-restore` → `response-wait-entry`, semantic.cljc:106-115) — still naming the emitter's own call-out reflection via its fresh key, not `:yin/call-out` (`cell-resources`, remote.cljc:524-543; `cursor-entry-key`, remote.cljc:556-562 keeps §7.5.3 sharing for co-waiters). Confirmed r2 behavior (link waits on the fixed link keys, remote.cljc:665-668 + `link-pair-resources` remote.cljc:565) is untouched.\n\n**Test extended past the migrated call** (test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:507-618, `a-retained-ffi-request-migrates-and-the-retry-resumes`): the program makes two calls — the migrated one and a new one. After the migrated call's response reaches its waiter through the emitter's pair (retry envelope verified landing verbatim on the emitter's call-in via the wire; response consumed via the route cell), the program's new call flows on the receiver's own pair: its request lands on the receiver's own call-in (`[\"world\"]`, :606-611) and nothing crosses to the emitter's call-in; the receiver's own bridge answers on its own call-out, and after the composition re-points its spent route at its own pair (the doc's separate-stores rule, :561-565), run 3 halts with \"world!\" and an empty wait-set. The routing assertions (:545-559) pin: no fixed stream keys in the lowered table, retry on the emitter's reflection, route cell naming the emitter's call-out. Debugging used a /tmp scratch script (deleted) — no repo files beyond the two slice-8 files.\n\n**Lane counts (focused, exact).**\n- JVM `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.ucf.remote-test`: Ran 18 tests containing 162 assertions — 0 failures, 0 errors.\n- Node (shadow-cljs build; `node target/node-tests.js --test=yin.vm.ucf.remote-test`): Ran 18 tests containing 162 assertions — 0 failures, 0 errors.\n- Dart (`flutter test test/cljd-out/yin/vm/ucf/remote-test_test.dart` on the `cljd`-compiled file): 18 of 18 passed — \"All tests passed!\".\n- Attribution: full-suite runs touched other namespaces only — Node full run: 7 failures, all `dao.stream.ws.node-test` (concurrent slice-5 ws/rpc work); Dart full run: 33 loading failures in demo/embed files plus `cljd/flutter.dart` IFnMixin analyzer noise from the shared cljd-out tree mid-flight (slice-5). None in `yin.vm.ucf.remote-test`.\n- Hygiene: cljstyle check clean, clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings, pure ASCII, ≤ 80 columns, no diagnostics; both slice-8 files still untracked, no git operations.\n\nStatus: COMPLETE","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
