{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc | sed -n '1,210p;740,885p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.remote-test\n     2\t  \"The slice 8 acceptance row\n     3\t   (`docs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md` slice 8;\n     4\t   `yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md` S7.4.3, S7.5.3, S7.11.1\n     5\t   'Reflection acceptance'): a REAL machine parked through the engine\n     6\t   on a `:stream-next` wait migrates with a kept cursor and resumes\n     7\t   equivalently in a fresh engine state through a reflection; forced\n     8\t   eviction yields `gap` with the source's own recovery cursor; a\n     9\t   kept cursor that cannot survive the channel codec refuses the lift\n    10\t   before any cell is published; a source `serve!` refuses is\n    11\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied`; an `attach!` that answers gone is\n    12\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming the stream at lower. Cursor cells are\n    13\t   minted and remapped across a whole frame set: two waiters on one\n    14\t   engine cell lift to one UCF cell and lower back shared, and\n    15\t   independent cells at one position stay independent (S7.5.3). The\n    16\t   remaining S7.4.3 variants -- `:put`, `:ffi`, `:ffi-request`,\n    17\t   `:link-request`, `:link-response`, `:install` -- round-trip\n    18\t   through stub `serve!`/`attach!` callbacks over the engine's own\n    19\t   wait-set shapes, since their proof is the shape of the bridge, not\n    20\t   the transport. The lowered waits the engine resolves at its own\n    21\t   fixed resource keys resume there for real: a retained\n    22\t   `:link-request` migrates and the engine's own poll retries it and\n    23\t   resumes on the response read at the fixed link keys; a retained\n    24\t   FFI request migrates, its retry appends at the fixed call-in key,\n    25\t   and the restored response wait -- `semantic-restore` parks it on\n    26\t   the receiver's fixed local call-out keys -- receives the retried\n    27\t   response the route cell carried.\"\n    28\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    29\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    30\t            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n    31\t            [dao.stream.remote :as remote]\n    32\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n    33\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    34\t            [yin.vm.linearize :as linearize]\n    35\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n    36\t            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n    37\t            [yin.vm.ucf.remote :as ucf.remote]))\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\t;; =============================================================================\n    41\t;; The toy: two in-process ring buffers as the channel (as\n    42\t;; dao.stream.remote-test), with a served-table `serve!` on top\n    43\t;; =============================================================================\n    44\t\n    45\t(defn- ring\n    46\t  [capacity]\n    47\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n    48\t    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ringbuffer\n    49\t                         :dao.stream.ringbuffer/capacity capacity})))\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\t(defn- toy\n    53\t  []\n    54\t  (let [ab (ring 64)\n    55\t        ba (ring 64)\n    56\t        cd {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n    57\t            :dao.stream/identity \"ucf-remote-toy\"}]\n    58\t    {:channel cd, :ab ab, :ba ba,\n    59\t     :a-end {:reader ba, :writer ab},\n    60\t     :b-end {:reader ab, :writer ba}}))\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\t(defn- served-peer\n    64\t  [t]\n    65\t  {:table (atom {})\n    66\t   :b-reader (:reader (:b-end t))\n    67\t   :b-writer (:writer (:b-end t))\n    68\t   :mirror (atom (:dao.stream/cursor\n    69\t                   (stream/cursor (:reader (:b-end t)) :dao.stream/oldest)))})\n    70\t\n    71\t\n    72\t(defn- serve-mirror!\n    73\t  \"One mirror step over everything pending on the toy's request\n    74\t   buffer.\"\n    75\t  [peer]\n    76\t  (swap! (:mirror peer)\n    77\t         #(remote/mirror-step @(:table peer) (:b-reader peer) %\n    78\t                              (:b-writer peer))))\n    79\t\n    80\t\n    81\t(defn- server\n    82\t  \"The exporter's `serve!` (dao.stream.remote.md S2.3): assigns a\n    83\t   stable identity to `h`, entering it in the peer's table under\n    84\t   `chan`, if it is not already served. The served surface defaults\n    85\t   to reader only; a stream the remote writes through -- a link\n    86\t   request stream the lowered retry appends to, a call-in stream the\n    87\t   retried FFI request lands on -- is served with the writer surface\n    88\t   too.\"\n    89\t  ([peer chan] (server peer chan #{:reader}))\n    90\t  ([peer chan surfaces]\n    91\t   (fn [h]\n    92\t     (if-let [existing (some (fn [[id e]] (when (= h (:handle e)) id))\n    93\t                             @(:table peer))]\n    94\t       {:dao.stream/identity existing, :dao.stream/channel chan}\n    95\t       (let [id (str (gensym \"seg\"))]\n    96\t         (swap! (:table peer) assoc id {:handle h, :surface surfaces})\n    97\t         {:dao.stream/identity id, :dao.stream/channel chan})))))\n    98\t\n    99\t\n   100\t(defn- attacher\n   101\t  [t]\n   102\t  (remote/attacher\n   103\t    {:dao.stream.remote/channels {(:channel t) (:a-end t)}}))\n   104\t\n   105\t\n   106\t;; =============================================================================\n   107\t;; The emitter side: a real machine parked through the engine\n   108\t;; =============================================================================\n   109\t\n   110\t(def ^:private secret\n   111\t  \"The capability secret the test composition gives its machines.\"\n   112\t  \"yin.vm.ucf.remote-test/capability-secret\")\n   113\t\n   114\t\n   115\t(defn- make-ring-stream\n   116\t  \"The ring-buffer `:make-stream` this composition gives its\n   117\t   machines -- `yin.vm.test-utils`'s choice, at test scale.\"\n   118\t  [capacity]\n   119\t  (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ringbuffer\n   120\t                       :dao.stream.ringbuffer/capacity capacity}))\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\t(defn- new-machine\n   124\t  \"A fresh semantic machine over that composition.\"\n   125\t  []\n   126\t  (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream make-ring-stream\n   127\t                       :capability-secret secret}))\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\t(def ^:private load-ast\n   131\t  \"The trusted fresh path: the AST linearizer behind the code loader.\"\n   132\t  (vm/fresh-code-loader (linearize/ast-loader semantic/vm-load-program)\n   133\t                        vm/ast-contract))\n   134\t\n   135\t\n   136\t(defn- var-ref\n   137\t  [n]\n   138\t  {:type :variable, :name n})\n   139\t\n   140\t\n   141\t(defn- let1\n   142\t  \"`((fn [param] body) init)`.\"\n   143\t  [param init body]\n   144\t  {:type :application,\n   145\t   :operator {:type :lambda, :params [param], :body body},\n   146\t   :operands [init]})\n   147\t\n   148\t\n   149\t(defn- reader-datoms\n   150\t  \"Make a stream of `capacity`, mint a cursor on it, read one value.\"\n   151\t  [capacity]\n   152\t  (vm/ast->datoms\n   153\t    (let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer capacity}\n   154\t          {:type :stream/next,\n   155\t           :source {:type :stream/cursor, :source (var-ref 's)}})))\n   156\t\n   157\t\n   158\t(defn- parked-reader\n   159\t  \"A real machine parked through the engine on a `:stream-next` wait\n   160\t   over a fresh ring buffer: the code datoms, the parked VM, its\n   161\t   wait-set entry, and the stream handle the entry polls.\"\n   162\t  [capacity]\n   163\t  (let [datoms (reader-datoms capacity)\n   164\t        parked (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine) datoms))\n   165\t        entry (first (:wait-set parked))]\n   166\t    [datoms parked entry\n   167\t     (get (:resources parked) (:stream-id entry))]))\n   168\t\n   169\t\n   170\t(defn- lit\n   171\t  [v]\n   172\t  {:type :literal, :value v})\n   173\t\n   174\t\n   175\t(defn- one-slot-stream\n   176\t  \"A stream that answers `full` while one value sits in it -- the one\n   177\t   append outcome a ring buffer never gives (a ringbuffer evicts),\n   178\t   without which no request stays retained. Reading the value frees\n   179\t   the slot. The descriptor answers ok, so the reflection's attach\n   180\t   probe is answerable.\"\n   181\t  [identity]\n   182\t  (let [slot (atom :empty)]\n   183\t    (reify\n   184\t      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   185\t      (descriptor\n   186\t        [_]\n   187\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok,\n   188\t         :dao.stream/identity identity,\n   189\t         :dao.stream/descriptor\n   190\t         {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel,\n   191\t          :dao.stream/identity identity}})\n   192\t\n   193\t\n   194\t      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   195\t\n   196\t      (cursor\n   197\t        [_ _anchor]\n   198\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok, :dao.stream/cursor 0})\n   199\t\n   200\t      (next\n   201\t        [_ cursor]\n   202\t        (if (and (= 0 cursor) (not= :empty @slot))\n   203\t          (let [v @slot]\n   204\t            (reset! slot :empty)\n   205\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok,\n   206\t             :dao.stream/value v, :dao.stream/cursor 1})\n   207\t          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}))\n   208\t\n   209\t\n   210\t      stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   740\t        attach! (stub-attach!)\n   741\t        [_datoms parked entry _src] (parked-reader 4)\n   742\t        cid (:id (:cursor-ref entry))\n   743\t        ;; a second waiter on the SAME engine cursor cell, as\n   744\t        ;; check-wait-set's shared-cursor co-waiters hold\n   745\t        second (assoc (registers-of entry)\n   746\t                      :reason :next,\n   747\t                      :stream-id (:stream-id entry),\n   748\t                      :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id cid},\n   749\t                      :pc 42)\n   750\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-frame serve! (:resources parked)\n   751\t                                      [entry second])]\n   752\t    (testing \"two waiters on one engine cell lift to one UCF cell\"\n   753\t      (is (= 1 (count (:yin.k/cells lifted))))\n   754\t      (let [[p1 p2] (:yin.k/pending lifted)]\n   755\t        (is (= (:yin.k/cell p1) (:yin.k/cell p2))\n   756\t            \"both waiters name the one cell\")))\n   757\t    (let [ctxs [(registers-of entry) (registers-of second)]\n   758\t          lowered (ucf.remote/lower-frame attach! (:yin.k/pending lifted)\n   759\t                                          (:yin.k/cells lifted) ctxs)\n   760\t          [e1 e2] (:entries lowered)\n   761\t          rs (:resources lowered)]\n   762\t      (testing \"and lower back into one shared cursor entry\"\n   763\t        (is (= (get-in e1 [:cursor-ref :id])\n   764\t               (get-in e2 [:cursor-ref :id]))\n   765\t            \"one cell id stands for the one entry\")\n   766\t        (is (= 1 (count (cursor-entries rs)))))\n   767\t      (testing \"each entry keeps its own register context\"\n   768\t        (is (= (:pc entry) (:pc e1)))\n   769\t        (is (= 42 (:pc e2)))))))\n   770\t\n   771\t\n   772\t(deftest independent-cells-at-one-position-stay-independent\n   773\t  (let [serve! (stub-serve! chan)\n   774\t        attach! (stub-attach!)\n   775\t        s (ring 8)\n   776\t        _ (stream/append! s \"v\")\n   777\t        c0 (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor s :dao.stream/oldest))\n   778\t        resources {:yin/s s,\n   779\t                   :yin/c1 {:stream-id :yin/s, :cursor c0},\n   780\t                   :yin/c2 {:stream-id :yin/s, :cursor c0}}\n   781\t        entry1 {:reason :next,\n   782\t                :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id :yin/c1},\n   783\t                :stream-id :yin/s}\n   784\t        entry2 {:reason :next,\n   785\t                :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id :yin/c2},\n   786\t                :stream-id :yin/s}\n   787\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-frame serve! resources\n   788\t                                      [entry1 entry2])]\n   789\t    (testing \"two engine cells at one position are two UCF cells\"\n   790\t      (is (= 2 (count (:yin.k/cells lifted)))\n   791\t          \"the aliasing a position-only encoding erases, kept\")\n   792\t      (let [[p1 p2] (:yin.k/pending lifted)]\n   793\t        (is (not= (:yin.k/cell p1) (:yin.k/cell p2)))\n   794\t        (is (= c0 (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells (:yin.k/cell p1)\n   795\t                                  :yin.k/position])))\n   796\t        (is (= c0 (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells (:yin.k/cell p2)\n   797\t                                  :yin.k/position])))))\n   798\t    (let [ctx {:segment 0, :pc 1, :env {}, :stack [], :k []}\n   799\t          lowered (ucf.remote/lower-frame attach! (:yin.k/pending lifted)\n   800\t                                          (:yin.k/cells lifted)\n   801\t                                          [ctx ctx])\n   802\t          [e1 e2] (:entries lowered)\n   803\t          rs (:resources lowered)]\n   804\t      (testing \"and lower into two independently advanceable entries\"\n   805\t        (is (not= (get-in e1 [:cursor-ref :id])\n   806\t                  (get-in e2 [:cursor-ref :id])))\n   807\t        (is (= 2 (count (cursor-entries rs))))\n   808\t        (is (= 1 (count (filter vector? (vals rs))))\n   809\t            \"one stream, so the two cells share one reflection\")))))\n   810\t\n   811\t\n   812\t(deftest a-refused-leaf-refuses-the-frame\n   813\t  (let [serve! (stub-serve! chan)\n   814\t        s (ring 4)\n   815\t        c0 (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor s :dao.stream/oldest))\n   816\t        resources {:yin/s s, :yin/c {:stream-id :yin/s, :cursor c0}}\n   817\t        good {:reason :next,\n   818\t              :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id :yin/c},\n   819\t              :stream-id :yin/s}]\n   820\t    (is (= :yin.k/undecodable\n   821\t           (:yin.k/status\n   822\t             (ucf.remote/lift-frame serve! resources\n   823\t                                    [good {:reason :bogus}])))\n   824\t        \"an unrecognized reason is total, S7.5.4\")\n   825\t    (is (= :yin.k/unsatisfied\n   826\t           (:yin.k/status\n   827\t             (ucf.remote/lift-frame (constantly nil) resources [good]))))))\n   828\t\n   829\t\n   830\t;; =============================================================================\n   831\t;; The remaining S7.4.3 variants round-trip, over the engine's shapes\n   832\t;; =============================================================================\n   833\t\n   834\t(deftest a-blocked-read-round-trips\n   835\t  (let [serve! (stub-serve! chan)\n   836\t        attach! (stub-attach!)\n   837\t        resources {:yin/s [:handle :s],\n   838\t                   :yin/c {:stream-id :yin/s, :cursor :kept-position}}\n   839\t        entry {:reason :next,\n   840\t               :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id :yin/c},\n   841\t               :stream-id :yin/s}\n   842\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! resources entry)]\n   843\t    (is (= {:yin.k/reason :next, :yin.k/cell :yin.k/c-0}\n   844\t           (:yin.k/pending lifted))\n   845\t        \"the cursor CELL id, S7.5.3 -- not a bare position\")\n   846\t    (is (= :kept-position\n   847\t           (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells :yin.k/c-0 :yin.k/position])))\n   848\t    (is (= #{:dao.stream.remote/v1}\n   849\t           (get-in lifted [:yin.k/requires :yin.k/cursor-profiles])))\n   850\t    (let [ctx {:segment 0, :pc 7, :env {}, :stack [], :k []}\n   851\t          lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! (:yin.k/pending lifted)\n   852\t                                            (:yin.k/cells lifted) ctx)\n   853\t          e (:entry lowered)]\n   854\t      (is (= :next (:reason e)))\n   855\t      (is (= 7 (:pc e)) \"the registers ride the lower\")\n   856\t      (is (= :yin.k/c-0 (get-in e [:cursor-ref :id])))\n   857\t      (is (contains? (:resources lowered) (:stream-id e)))\n   858\t      (is (= :kept-position\n   859\t             (get-in lowered [:resources (get-in e [:cursor-ref :id])\n   860\t                              :cursor]))))))\n   861\t\n   862\t\n   863\t(deftest put-round-trips\n   864\t  (let [serve! (stub-serve! chan)\n   865\t        attach! (stub-attach!)\n   866\t        resources {:yin/w [:handle :w]}\n   867\t        entry {:reason :put, :stream-id :yin/w, :datom \"hello\"}\n   868\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! resources entry)]\n   869\t    (is (= :put (get-in lifted [:yin.k/pending :yin.k/reason])))\n   870\t    (is (= \"hello\" (get-in lifted [:yin.k/pending :yin.k/value]))\n   871\t        \"the retained :datom -- a retry appends THIS\")\n   872\t    (is (empty? (:yin.k/cells lifted))\n   873\t        \"a put wait names a stream, never a cursor cell\")\n   874\t    (is (empty? (:yin.k/requires lifted)))\n   875\t    (let [ctx {:segment 0, :pc 3, :env {}, :stack [], :k []}\n   876\t          lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! (:yin.k/pending lifted)\n   877\t                                            (:yin.k/cells lifted) ctx)\n   878\t          e (:entry lowered)]\n   879\t      (is (= :put (:reason e)))\n   880\t      (is (= \"hello\" (:datom e)))\n   881\t      (is (contains? (:resources lowered) (:stream-id e))\n   882\t          \"the target is a fresh reflection resource\"))))\n   883\t\n   884\t\n   885\t(deftest ffi-sent-round-trips\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | sed -n '650,730p'; rg -n '7.5.3|sharing|re-point' docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | sed -n '650,730p'; rg -n '7.5.3|sharing|re-point' docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md\"","aggregated_output":"   650\t                   :yin.link/format :yin.debruijn.code\n   651\t                   :yin.link/contract \"b2\"}   ; rebuilt verbatim\n   652\t :yin.k/request   {:dao.stream/identity ... :dao.stream/descriptor ...}\n   653\t :yin.k/response  {:dao.stream/identity ... :dao.stream/descriptor ...}\n   654\t :yin.k/cell      :yin.k/c-31}            ; response cell, minted newest\n   655\t                                          ; before the request is appended\n   656\t\n   657\t;; module link, awaiting the correlated response (request appended ok)\n   658\t{:yin.k/reason    :link-response\n   659\t :yin.k/link-id   [:t0 7]\n   660\t :yin.k/response  {:dao.stream/identity ... :dao.stream/descriptor ...}\n   661\t :yin.k/cell      :yin.k/c-31}            ; the kept cell, at its kept\n   662\t                                          ; position\n   663\t\n   664\t;; module install (a matching ok discharged; the child runs)\n   665\t{:yin.k/reason    :install\n   666\t :yin.k/name      'foo}\n   667\t```\n   668\t\n   669\tFour rules fix the exchange. The link id is the pair `[origin\n   670\tcounter]`, scoped to the link pair, not to a VM: several tasks share\n   671\tone response stream, `origin` is a task origin tag the scheduler mints\n   672\tfrom its own counter and never reuses, and `counter` is the task's\n   673\tengine gensym, so no two requests on one pair share an id. The response\n   674\tcursor is minted `:dao.stream/newest` before the request is appended --\n   675\tthe `dao.stream.md` *Cursors* rule for observing events caused by an\n   676\toperation -- so a response that lands before the cursor exists is not\n   677\tskipped. `:link-request` carries everything needed to rebuild the\n   678\tenvelope, `:link-response` carries the response descriptor and the kept\n   679\tcell; a `full` append keeps the request state, retains the envelope\n   680\tverbatim, and retries on the next poll, the `:ffi-request` discipline.\n   681\tAnd the poll restores only on exact correlation: the entry advances\n   682\tpast every response whose `:yin.link/id` is not its own, keeping its\n   683\tcursor at the first unconsumed position -- the per-cell round-order\n   684\tdiscipline section 7.5.3 already gives shared cursors -- and skips\n   685\tduplicate, late, and unknown responses, each skip a telemetry\n   686\tdiagnostic that consumes nothing but the cursor position. A matching\n   687\trefusal, or a failed discharge, resumes the program with the refusal\n   688\traised as the effect's error, the way an `:ffi` `error` raises; a\n   689\tcomposition that abandons a link raises the reason the same way and\n   690\tretires the id. A matching `ok` makes the entry `:install`, and no task\n   691\tis restored until the install reaches `linked` or `refused`: `linked`\n   692\trestores every waiter with the required module's symbol as its value,\n   693\t`refused` with the refusal as the effect's error. On `gap` the honest\n   694\toutcome is a `gap`, and the composition's policy decides.\n   695\t\n   696\t## §7.5 Recursive portable encoding (blocker 2)\n   697\t\n   698\t### 7.5.1 A disjoint tagged grammar\n   699\t\n   700\tEncoding is one total function `encode : value × path → outcome`, applied\n   701\trecursively to every value reachable from the frame: accumulator, operand\n   702\tstack, environment values, every frame in K, parked records, and the store\n   703\tslice of §7.6.2. The outcome is either the portable form or a refusal naming\n   704\tthe path.\n   705\t\n   706\tThe first draft encoded markers as ordinary maps — `{:yin.k/primitive '+}`,\n   707\t`{:yin.k/ref addr}` — while passing program map literals through in their\n   708\tnatural shape. That is ambiguous to everyone: §2.5 admits map literals,\n   709\tso a program can *contain* `{:yin.k/primitive '+}`, and a decoder cannot tell\n   710\tan encoder's marker from a program's data. The grammar here is disjoint by\n   711\tconstruction: **every map at an encoded-value position is a UCF marker**, and\n   712\ta program's own maps are always wrapped.\n   713\t\n   714\t| Encoded form | Tag | Contents | Decodes to |\n   715\t|---|---|---|---|\n   716\t| scalars: nil, boolean, number, string, keyword, symbol | — | themselves (never a map; cannot forge a marker) | themselves |\n   717\t| vector, list, set | — | same shape, elements recursively encoded (never a map) | same shape, elements decoded |\n   718\t| literal map | `:yin.k/literal` | `:yin.k/entries [k₁ v₁ k₂ v₂ …]`, keys and values recursively encoded | the map, keys and values decoded |\n   719\t| closure | `:yin.k/closure` | `:yin.k/segment addr :yin.k/entry pc :yin.k/params […] :yin.k/env {encoded}` | `{:type :closure …}` (§2.4) |\n   720\t| reified continuation | `:yin.k/frame` | a nested frame (§7.4.1), recursively | `{:type :reified-continuation …}` |\n   721\t| parked continuation | `:yin.k/frame` | a nested frame plus `:yin.k/parked-id` | `{:type :parked-continuation …}` |\n   722\t| primitive | `:yin.k/primitive` | `:yin.k/name sym` | the named function, after profile check (§7.5.2) |\n   723\t| stream reference | `:yin.k/stream` | `:dao.stream/identity … :dao.stream/descriptor …` | an attached handle, under a fresh store key |\n   724\t| cursor reference | `:yin.k/cursor-ref` | `:yin.k/cell cell-id` | a store cursor entry for that cell, §7.5.3 |\n   725\t| shared subvalue | `:yin.k/ref` | `:yin.k/id addr` | the table entry at `addr`, §7.5.3 |\n   726\t| anything else | — | — | **refused**: `:yin.k/non-portable` |\n   727\t\n   728\tWhy the wrapping is total rather than an \"escaping rule\" for suspicious\n   729\tshapes: a literal map is wrapped *wherever it occurs and whatever it\n   730\tcontains* — including one that happens to read `{:yin.k/tag …}` — and the\n78:(sharing thresholds differ, §7.5.3), so the encodings address differently,\n109: :yin.k/values      {…}                        ; §7.5.3  shared subvalues, by content address\n110: :yin.k/cells       {…}                        ; §7.5.3  cursor cells: logical identity + position\n385:encodings legitimately differ (§7.5.3), so `:yin.k/id` is *not* what custody,\n558: :yin.k/cell     :yin.k/c-17}          ; the cursor CELL id, §7.5.3 — not a bare position\n572: :yin.k/cell       :yin.k/c-23         ; the response cursor cell, §7.5.3, at its KEPT position}\n591:  waiters sharing a cell consume successive values — are preserved on the\n621:  id remapped per §7.5.3), while calls the resumed program makes *after*\n643:7.5.3:\n684:discipline section 7.5.3 already gives shared cursors -- and skips\n724:| cursor reference | `:yin.k/cursor-ref` | `:yin.k/cell cell-id` | a store cursor entry for that cell, §7.5.3 |\n725:| shared subvalue | `:yin.k/ref` | `:yin.k/id addr` | the table entry at `addr`, §7.5.3 |\n885:### 7.5.3 Sharing, cells, and cycles\n900:  for correctness of sharing.\n1098:7.5.3 move with them.\n1107:the carried slice, the remapped cells of §7.5.3, and the resumer's FFI pair\n1113:keys (cursor cells per §7.5.3, stream handles per §7.4.3), and non-resource\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
