{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | sed -n '916,948p'; nl -ba test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc | sed -n '324,354p'; rg -n 'response-cell|co-wait|route' test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"   916\t**Cursor cells.** A cursor is *observable state with aliasing*: two distinct\n   917\tcursor refs may sit at the same position and yet be independently\n   918\tadvanceable store entries, while repeated refs to one cursor ref must\n   919\tadvance together — `check-wait-set` advances a shared cursor ref before\n   920\tpolling the next waiter, so waiters on one ref read successive values, and\n   921\twaiters on two refs at the same position read the same next value\n   922\t(`yin.vm.engine`, `check-wait-set`). A position-only encoding erases\n   923\texactly this distinction: two cells at one position would collapse, and\n   924\ttheir independent advancement would be lost. The encoding therefore carries\n   925\t**logical cursor cells** separately from position content:\n   926\t\n   927\t```clojure\n   928\t:yin.k/cells {:yin.k/c-17 {:yin.k/stream   {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/stream …}\n   929\t                           :yin.k/position <opaque, exactly as the transport minted it>}}\n   930\t;; values reference cells, never positions:\n   931\t{:yin.k/tag :yin.k/cursor-ref :yin.k/cell :yin.k/c-17}\n   932\t```\n   933\t\n   934\tCell ids are minted by the emitter (stable within one lift; remapped on\n   935\tlowering) and are *not* content-addressed — a cell is a local identity, like\n   936\ta tempid, and deduplicating cells by their contents is precisely the aliasing\n   937\terasure this structure exists to prevent. On lowering, each cell becomes a\n   938\tfresh store cursor entry seeded with its carried position; every\n   939\t`:yin.k/cursor-ref` to it remaps to that entry; two refs to one cell share\n   940\tone entry and one ref per cell keeps its own. The FFI response cell of\n   941\t§7.4.3 is a cell like any other.\n   942\t\n   943\t**Cells lower into the private resource table (linker M4).** Specified by\n   944\t`yin.vm.linker.md` and implemented in M4. The lowering rule above -- each\n   945\tcell becomes a fresh store cursor entry -- is amended by the resource\n   946\tsplit of `yin.vm.linker.md` 7.3: each cell becomes a cursor entry in the\n   947\treceiver's private `:resources` table, seeded with its carried position,\n   948\tand every `:yin.k/cursor-ref` to it remaps to that entry; two refs to one\n   324\t(defn- quiesced-receiver\n   325\t  \"The fresh engine state a lower installs into: a real machine over\n   326\t   the same code image, quiesced, holding the lowered resource table\n   327\t   and the lowered wait-set entry -- nothing of the emitter's state\n   328\t   but the code image and the registers the entry carries.\"\n   329\t  ([datoms lowered] (quiesced-receiver datoms lowered (new-machine)))\n   330\t  ([datoms lowered machine]\n   331\t   (assoc (load-ast machine datoms)\n   332\t          :control nil, :k nil,\n   333\t          :value :yin/blocked, :blocked? true, :halted? false,\n   334\t          :wait-set [(:entry lowered)],\n   335\t          :resources (:resources lowered))))\n   336\t\n   337\t\n   338\t(defn- cursor-entries\n   339\t  \"The cursor entries of a lowered resource table: maps keyed by the\n   340\t   UCF cell ids, each carrying its stream id and kept cursor.\"\n   341\t  [table]\n   342\t  (into {} (filter (fn [[_ v]] (and (map? v) (contains? v :stream-id))))\n   343\t        table))\n   344\t\n   345\t\n   346\t;; =============================================================================\n   347\t;; The acceptance row: a real parked machine migrates and resumes\n   348\t;; =============================================================================\n   349\t\n   350\t(deftest migrates-a-real-parked-machine-and-resumes\n   351\t  (let [t (toy)\n   352\t        peer (served-peer t)\n   353\t        serve! (server peer (:channel t))\n   354\t        attach! (attacher t)\n27:   response the route cell carried.\"\n306:   where a future call routes.\"\n544:               ;; through the route and parks the restored response\n562:        ;; state, so the composition re-points its spent route at its\n573:    (testing \"the lift carries the response route as a cell\"\n574:      (is (= :yin.k/c-0 (:yin.k/response-cell pending)))\n578:    (testing \"the lower routes the outstanding call, not the pair\"\n586:      (let [route (get rs vm/call-out-cursor-key)]\n587:        (is (= kept (:cursor route))\n588:            \"the route cell lowers as the restored wait's cursor entry\")\n589:        (is (not= vm/call-out-stream-key (:stream-id route))\n591:        (is (contains? rs (:stream-id route))\n744:        ;; check-wait-set's shared-cursor co-waiters hold\n931:    (is (= :yin.k/c-0 (:yin.k/response-cell pending))\n932:        \"the response route rides as a cell\")\n934:        \"the route cell at the emitter's kept call-out position\")\n937:        \"the frame carries a cursor profile: the route is a cell\")\n957:      (let [route (get rs vm/call-out-cursor-key)\n958:            route-id (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells :yin.k/c-0\n961:        (is (= 2 (:cursor route))\n962:            \"the route cell lowers as the restored wait's cursor entry\")\n963:        (is (= [:reflection-of route-id] (get rs (:stream-id route)))\n965:        (is (not= vm/call-out-stream-key (:stream-id route)))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
